---
import DocsLayout from '../layouts/DocsLayout.astro';
import { stylesheets } from '../data/stylesheets.js';
import reference from './generated-reference.json';
import pkg from '../../../package.json';
const base=import.meta.env.BASE_URL;
const sections=[{id:'files',title:'Stylesheet files'},{id:'attributes',title:'Attribute API'},{id:'attribute-contracts',title:'Attribute usage rules'},{id:'boundaries',title:'Scope and behaviour'},{id:'related',title:'Detailed reference'}];
const usageLabels={targets:'Supported targets',inheritance:'Inheritance',localOverride:'Local overrides and resets',dependencies:'Dependencies',limitations:'Limits and combinations with no effect'};
function fileDescription(file) {
  const descriptions={
    'reva.button-materials.css':'Optional action-only solid, glass, veil, soft and liquid materials; load after the core.',
    'reva.button-materials.scoped.css':'Optional action-only materials inside .reva; load after the scoped core.',
    'reva.css':'Complete readable global stylesheet. Recommended starting point.',
    'reva.tokens.css':'Theme, palette and shared setting definitions.',
    'reva.base.css':'Native element styling. Depends on token definitions.',
    'reva.components.css':'Component bundle plus shared utilities. Depends on tokens and base.',
    'reva.scoped.css':'Complete styling scoped to .reva boundaries.',
    'reva.card-grid.css':'Container-responsive three-region cards with subgrid enhancement; included in the complete builds. Modular use requires tokens, base, components and card patterns.',
    'reva.gallery.css':'Native scroll-snap gallery with fragment navigation; included in the complete builds. Modular use requires tokens and base.',
    'reva.scrolling.css':'Native fragment scrolling and destination emphasis; included in the complete builds. Uses shared motion tokens.',
    'reva.scroll-top.css':'Scroll-to-top link presentation; included in the complete builds. Modular use requires tokens, base and scrolling.',
    'reva.hero.css':'Optional semantic hero layout and typography; load after global core and match material extensions.',
    'reva.hero.scoped.css':'Optional hero layout inside .reva; load after scoped core.',
    'reva.gradients.css':'Optional material/background gradient effects; inherited accent and motion, preference fallbacks.',
    'reva.gradients.scoped.css':'Optional gradient effects inside .reva; load after scoped core.',
    'reva.reading-progress.css':'Optional native page-scroll position bar; load after global core. Not included in the core.',
    'reva.reading-progress.scoped.css':'Optional page-scroll position bar within .reva; load after scoped core. Still tracks the root page.',
    'reva.scroll-motion.css':'Optional scroll-driven card entrance motion; load after the global core. Static content is the fallback.',
    'reva.scroll-motion.scoped.css':'Optional scroll-driven card entrance motion inside .reva; load after reva.scoped.css.',
    'reva.transitions.css':'Optional same-origin cross-document view transitions; load on both destinations. Document-level only, with no scoped equivalent.',
    'reva.motion.css':'Optional opening/closing motion for native popovers and dialogs; load after the global core.',
    'reva.motion.scoped.css':'Optional scoped overlay motion; load after reva.scoped.css.',
    'reva.glass.css':'Optional global glass extension; load after the global core.',
    'reva.glass.scoped.css':'Optional scoped glass extension; load after reva.scoped.css.',
    'reva.veil.css':'Optional Veil material: diffused perimeter colour and contained contours without blur. Load after the global core.',
    'reva.veil.scoped.css':'Optional scoped Veil material; load after reva.scoped.css.'
  };
  return descriptions[file] || 'Component-specific styling. Load its token/base dependencies and any required shared utilities.';
}
---
<DocsLayout title="API reference" active="reference" sections={sections}>
<p class="doc-kicker">REFERENCE</p><h1>API reference</h1>
<p class="doc-lead">The current CSS and HTML interface for RevaCSS {pkg.version}. Attribute values below come from the option manifest used by the build.</p>
<p>Use the <a href={base+'guide/'}>guide</a> for setup and the <a href={base+'reference/components/'}>component API</a> for exact hooks. The API describes implemented features, not a release-validation guarantee.</p>
<section id="files"><h2>Stylesheet files</h2><p>Start with one complete build: global or scoped. Do not combine both. Load the matching Glass or Veil extension afterward when needed.</p>
<div class="table-scroll" role="region" aria-label="Stylesheet entry points" tabindex="0"><table><caption>Generated CSS files</caption><thead><tr><th scope="col">File</th><th scope="col">Purpose</th></tr></thead><tbody>
<tr><th scope="row"><code>reva.min.css</code></th><td>Minified equivalent of the complete global stylesheet.</td></tr>
{stylesheets.map(file=><tr><th scope="row"><code>{file}</code></th><td>{fileDescription(file)}</td></tr>)}
<tr><th scope="row"><code>reva-fonts.css</code></th><td>Optional Manrope font declarations; copy its adjacent fonts directory.</td></tr>
</tbody></table></div>
<p>The generated icons directory contains individual SVG files and <code>icons/reva.svg</code>. <a href={base+'icons/'}>See icon usage and downloads.</a></p>
<p>Standalone modules are not a replacement for common dependencies. The complete build includes shared preference utilities; modular consumers must preserve the corresponding behaviours.</p></section>
<section id="attributes"><h2>Shared attribute API</h2><p>Set shared appearance attributes on html, a parent section, or a .reva boundary. Local settings such as data-table-sticky apply only to their documented wrapper. A nearer valid value configures supported descendants, subject to component precedence and preference rules. Use the detailed usage rules below for resets and material boundaries; unsupported values are not a general inheritance or reset mechanism.</p>
<div class="table-scroll" role="region" aria-label="Shared attribute API" tabindex="0"><table class="attribute-api"><caption>{Object.keys(reference.options).length} settings from tokens/options.json</caption><thead><tr><th scope="col">Attribute</th><th scope="col">Values</th><th scope="col">Unconfigured default</th><th scope="col">Targets and meaning</th></tr></thead><tbody>
{Object.entries(reference.options).map(([name,opt])=><tr><th scope="row"><a href={base+'attributes/#'+name}><code>data-{name}</code></a></th><td>{opt.values.join(' · ')}</td><td><code>{opt.default}</code></td><td>{opt.affects}</td></tr>)}
</tbody></table></div>
<p><code>data-variant</code> configures buttons, action inputs, .button links, badges and alerts. <code>data-appearance</code> configures only badges and alerts. Existing semantic button classes override inherited variants; a valid action-level variant overrides those classes. Material and fill remain separate settings.</p></section>
<section id="attribute-contracts"><h2>Attribute usage rules</h2>
<p>Omission keeps the inherited setting within the current boundary, or the initialized default when none applies. Default descriptions are not necessarily accepted values. There is no universal reset value. Unsupported values are not reliable resets: an unsupported material value can stop its parent scope without activating a replacement. Local resets and accessibility preferences have the setting-specific rules below.</p>
{Object.entries(reference.options).map(([name,option])=><details id={'usage-'+name}><summary><code>data-{name}</code> usage</summary><dl>{Object.entries(usageLabels).map(([field,label])=><><dt>{label}</dt><dd>{option.usage?.[field] || 'Consult the matching component reference.'}</dd></>)}</dl></details>)}
</section>
<section id="boundaries"><h2>Scope and behavioural boundaries</h2><p>Each .reva boundary installs defaults. Configure the boundary itself or its descendants. CSS scope does not provide Shadow DOM isolation, and overlay markup must remain in its boundary.</p><p>The core relies on modern CSS including light-dark(), color-mix(), :has() and @scope. Native popovers are required for the top-menu interaction. Some enhancements have component-specific fallbacks; do not assume a complete legacy-browser fallback.</p><p>CSS does not supply routing, data loading, validation messages or arbitrary focus management. See <a href={base+'guide/accessibility/'}>behaviour and accessibility</a>.</p></section>
<section id="related"><h2>Detailed reference</h2><ul><li><a href={base+'reference/components/'}>Component classes, native states and dependencies</a></li><li><a href={base+'reference/tokens/'}>CSS tokens and override examples</a></li><li><a href={base+'attributes/'}>Live HTML examples for every shared attribute</a></li></ul></section>
</DocsLayout>
<style>.attribute-api { min-inline-size:46rem; } @media print { .attribute-api { min-inline-size:0; } }</style>
